WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.292
Let's practise one line between lessons.

00:02.292 --> 00:06.542
We'll choose a recording, make a short exercise, and save our

00:06.542 --> 00:06.917
notes.

00:06.917 --> 00:12.042
You can pause this video at any step.

00:12.042 --> 00:16.083
On the Discover page, click Start with my own recording.

00:16.083 --> 00:17.333
Audio Lab opens.

00:17.333 --> 00:23.375
You can also choose Audio Lab from the top menu.

00:23.375 --> 00:26.792
Under Your recording, find Choose local reference audio.

00:26.792 --> 00:31.458
Click the file chooser and select a recording you have permission

00:31.458 --> 00:34.333
to use.

00:34.333 --> 00:37.708
Check that the filename and an audio player appear.

00:37.708 --> 00:43.458
The file stays in this tab; it is not uploaded.

00:43.458 --> 00:47.125
Press the triangular Play button and listen once.

00:47.125 --> 00:52.167
Our short example is synthetic: a workflow demonstration, not an accent

00:52.167 --> 00:53.625
model.

00:53.625 --> 00:57.167
Discover the joy of phonetics.

00:57.167 --> 00:59.792
Click Use this reference in Coach.

00:59.792 --> 01:04.583
Coach Workspace opens with the filename in the recording reference field.

01:04.583 --> 01:08.333
Leave Archive sample empty.

01:08.333 --> 01:12.667
In Short phrase or scene line, type Discover the joy of

01:12.667 --> 01:15.083
phonetics.

01:15.083 --> 01:19.250
In Teaching context, name your practice: Invitation practice, between

01:19.250 --> 01:19.708
lessons.

01:19.708 --> 01:25.917
This is a session title, not an account name.

01:25.917 --> 01:28.708
The next field is called Teaching task.

01:28.708 --> 01:33.125
Use it for your intention: Invite a colleague to explore the

01:33.125 --> 01:35.542
resource.

01:35.542 --> 01:40.667
In Sound target one, write Compare emphasis on JOY and PHONETICS.

01:40.667 --> 01:45.750
We are exploring one performance choice, not trying to copy an

01:45.750 --> 01:48.708
entire accent.

01:48.708 --> 01:52.417
Leave targets two and three blank for this first exercise.

01:52.417 --> 01:57.750
You can add another focus later with your teacher.

01:57.750 --> 01:58.917
Click Build drill.

01:58.917 --> 02:02.833
Your phrase and target appear in the third panel, Drill.

02:02.833 --> 02:09.167
This is a starting structure, not an analysis of your voice.

02:09.167 --> 02:13.750
Click inside the drill text and add these steps: Listen once.

02:13.750 --> 02:16.708
Say the line with emphasis on JOY.

02:16.708 --> 02:21.625
Then say it with emphasis on PHONETICS.

02:21.625 --> 02:25.583
Now say the whole line to an imagined colleague.

02:25.583 --> 02:28.208
Which emphasis better serves your invitation?

02:28.208 --> 02:30.833
Pause the video and try both.

02:30.833 --> 02:39.500
There is no automatic right answer.

02:39.500 --> 02:42.792
You do not need to record yourself to finish.

02:42.792 --> 02:46.792
If you want to explore the optional recorder, click Listen or

02:46.792 --> 02:50.250
record a practice take.

02:50.250 --> 02:53.542
In Audio Lab, scroll down to Record locally.

02:53.542 --> 02:58.042
This video shows the controls only; it does not turn on

02:58.042 --> 03:02.917
your microphone or claim a recorded take.

03:02.917 --> 03:06.750
Choose Coach in the top menu to return to your exercise.

03:06.750 --> 03:10.500
Your draft is still there.

03:10.500 --> 03:13.000
Scroll to Observations and next changes.

03:13.000 --> 03:17.583
Write one thing you actually heard and one question for your

03:17.583 --> 03:17.958
teacher.

03:17.958 --> 03:24.583
Our screen shows an example question, not a real learner result.

03:24.583 --> 03:28.958
Leave Expert feedback blank unless your teacher has given comments and

03:28.958 --> 03:30.542
permission to keep them.

03:30.542 --> 03:36.125
Skip the optional ratings if they are not useful.

03:36.125 --> 03:39.333
Return to the Drill panel and click Save session.

03:39.333 --> 03:43.875
Check for Session saved in this browser.

03:43.875 --> 03:45.542
Scroll to Saved sessions.

03:45.542 --> 03:47.583
Your named entry should appear.

03:47.583 --> 03:54.125
Click Open to return to that saved version in this browser.

03:54.125 --> 03:58.708
For ordinary exercise text, click Copy drill, then paste it into

03:58.708 --> 03:59.958
your own notes.

03:59.958 --> 04:04.500
It copies the drill, not your audio or all the session

04:04.500 --> 04:06.958
fields.

04:06.958 --> 04:11.583
For a structured backup, go to the top of Coach Workspace

04:11.583 --> 04:13.292
and click Export session.

04:13.292 --> 04:19.542
Your browser downloads a JSON file containing the session notes.

04:19.542 --> 04:24.292
This is a data file, not a PDF or an audio

04:24.292 --> 04:24.750
recording.

04:24.750 --> 04:26.917
Keep the original audio separately.

04:26.917 --> 04:32.833
Coach has no import button for this single-session file.

04:32.833 --> 04:37.375
Saved sessions belong to this browser, not an online account.

04:37.375 --> 04:42.375
Do not rely on them surviving cleared browser data or appearing

04:42.375 --> 04:43.750
on another device.

04:43.750 --> 04:47.583
Keep your exported files.

04:47.583 --> 04:51.792
After reloading, choose your audio file again in Audio Lab.

04:51.792 --> 04:57.208
Review your notes before sharing them with anyone.

04:57.208 --> 05:00.625
Bring your observation and question to the next lesson.

05:00.625 --> 05:06.500
Keep your own voice, and choose what helps your performance.
